# 14. Typography Usage Rules

## Display

Used primarily on:

- public hero
- major marketing statements
- major storytelling sections

Avoid on dense application screens.

## H1

One primary page heading.

## H2

Major page sections.

## H3/H4

Subsections and grouped content.

## Body

Default application content.

## Metadata

Use for:

- timestamps
- IDs
- compact table metadata
- secondary labels

Metadata must remain readable and must not be used as the primary information hierarchy.

---

# 15. Typography Constraints

Do not:

- use more than the approved weight range without explicit design-system revision
- mix unrelated typefaces
- use uppercase everywhere
- use giant text in operational dashboards
- use tiny text to fit more data
- create per-page typography scales

