# 21. Touch Targets

Interactive targets should generally provide at least:

```text
44px × 44px
```

This applies especially to:

- mobile navigation
- icon buttons
- close controls
- menu controls
- pagination controls
- action icons

Visual icon size may be smaller than the interactive hit area.

---

# 22. Iconography

Use one coherent icon family.

Icon rules:

- stroke-based icons are preferred
- consistent stroke weight
- no mixing unrelated icon styles
- no decorative icon overload
- icons must support meaning
- icons must not replace labels when the meaning is ambiguous

Recommended functional sizes:

```text
12px — metadata/inline
14px — compact controls
16px — standard controls
18px — navigation
20px — prominent controls
24px — major feature icons
32px+ — editorial/marketing usage
```

