# 94. Non-Negotiable Invariants

1. Manrope remains the canonical product typeface.
2. Soft Intelligence remains the canonical design identity.
3. Warm light is the default appearance.
4. Dark mode is a charcoal counterpart, not an inversion.
5. `#6F7F63` remains the primary light-theme accent unless the design system is explicitly revised.
6. All three roles use one visual system.
7. AI has a deeper layer but is not neon/cyberpunk.
8. Semantic colors must be used for state.
9. Arbitrary page-level colors are prohibited.
10. Arbitrary page-level spacing systems are prohibited.
11. Component geometry comes from the shared system.
12. Motion remains subtle and purposeful.
13. Reduced motion is supported.
14. Accessibility is part of the token contract.
15. Tokens do not own canonical application state.
16. Frontend does not infer backend authorization from token state.
17. Stitch prompts should consume the canonical system rather than inventing a competing one.
18. No silent design-system changes.

